package main

// qr_table.go -- the inputpad's QR symbol, as a module table.
//
// GENERATED FILE, DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.  Produced by .tmp/gen_qr.py, which
// calls segno 1.6.6 (a reference ISO/IEC 18004 implementation) with:
//
//     payload     'kvm'
//     version     27      (125 x 125 modules)
//     ECC level   M       (~15%% damage tolerated)
//     mode        byte
//     mask        0       (segno's penalty-minimal choice)
//
// WHY A TABLE AND NOT A COMPUTED SYMBOL: qr.go is an unfinished from-scratch
// encoder -- its geometry is right but its codeword stream does not yet match
// a reference, so it must not paint the pad. A table from a reference
// implementation IS a real symbol a phone can scan; it just cannot be edited.
// Regenerate with the script, never by hand: a single flipped module in the
// payload area is a silent corruption that still looks like a QR code.
//
// LAYOUT: qrSize modules square, painted FLUSH at the canvas's top-left cell,
// one module per cell. The 128-cell pad therefore leaves exactly 3 cells of
// white quiet zone on the RIGHT and BOTTOM edges (128 - 125), which is the
// user's requested margin ("让右侧还有下方留出白边").

const qrSize = 125

